ibmveth_pool_resize.py
======================

Description
-----------
Validates that the IBM Virtual Ethernet (ibmveth) driver correctly handles
resizing each receive-buffer pool (pool0 through pool4) to 65536 bytes while
background flood-ping traffic is running, with no kernel call traces or OOM
events.

The ibmveth driver exposes five receive-buffer pools via sysfs:

  /sys/class/net/<iface>/device/pool<N>/size    - buffer size in bytes (r/w)

This test writes a target value (default 65536) to each pool's size knob one
at a time, validates ping connectivity to the peer after each resize, scans
dmesg for call traces or OOM events, then restores the original value before
moving on to the next pool.


Parameters
----------
See ibmveth_pool_resize.yaml for the configuration template.

Parameter       Description                                    Notes
-----------     -------------------------------------------    -----------------
interface       ibmveth interface name or MAC address          REQUIRED
                  e.g.  eth0  or  56:44:AB:CD:12:34

host_ip         IP address to assign to the interface          REQUIRED
                  e.g.  192.168.10.1

netmask         Netmask for host_ip                            REQUIRED
                  e.g.  255.255.255.0

peer_ip         Peer machine IP address (used for ping)        REQUIRED
                  e.g.  192.168.10.2

peer_user       SSH username on the peer                       default: root
                  e.g.  root

peer_password   SSH password on the peer                       REQUIRED
                  e.g.  mysecretpassword

ping_count      Total packets for background flood-ping        default: 1000000
                  e.g.  100000

pool_size       Buffer size in bytes written to each           default: 65536
                pool's size sysfs knob
                  e.g.  65536


How to find parameter values
-----------------------------
interface:
  Run:  ip link show
  Look for interfaces with driver ibmveth:
        ls -l /sys/class/net/*/device/driver | grep ibmveth
  Use the interface name (e.g. eth0) or its MAC address from:
        ip link show eth0 | awk '/ether/{print $2}'

host_ip / netmask:
  Assign an IP on the same subnet as peer_ip.
  Example: if peer is 192.168.10.2/24, set host_ip=192.168.10.1 netmask=255.255.255.0

peer_ip:
  IP address of the remote peer machine used for flood-ping and SSH.
  Ensure the peer is reachable and SSH access is configured.

ping_count:
  Number of ICMP packets sent during the test. Higher values give longer
  traffic duration across all pool resizes. Default 1000000 is sufficient
  for a full 5-pool test run.
